War is a collection of brutal realities and of ways the human condition can be brought to extremes. When the WWII combat veterans came home everyone's story was different, yet sounded the same. After a while no-one was really listening because they all sounded similar and people mostly just wanted to forget their epic journey and have a good life. But it was these heroes that gave us this good life. What is not recorded is forgotten and these heroes stories should never be forgotten. Especially if you knew them and just let their story pass into the shadows of lost time.
Thereafter these combat veterans slipped into silence. But the look in their eyes where they appear to be looking out but only see the disaster in their mind was the tell and the history that I am now writing about. So many years have gone by and now this generation is totally slipping into flickering hints of ghost tales in vanished time. I hope this book I have been given the honor and privilege to write will be appreciated by the next generation and our future heroes."­
ªKathy, Ruth and Tommy were pupils at Hailsham - an idyllic establishment situated deep in the English countryside. The children there were tenderly sheltered from the outside world, brought up to believe they were special, and that their personal welfare was crucial. But for what reason were they really there? It is only years later that Kathy, now aged 31, finally allows herself to yield to the pull of memory. What unfolds is the haunting story of how Kathy, Ruth and Tommy, slowly come to face the truth about their seemingly happy childhoods - and about their futures. Never Let Me Go is a uniquely moving novel, charged throughout with a sense of the fragility of our lives."±
